# pabrik cross-platform line-ending policy.
#
# Force LF (Unix) line endings for all source files. Without this,
# Windows Git with `core.autocrlf=true` (the default) checks out
# text files with CRLF endings. The repo's static-contract tests
# read source files at runtime and use literal "\n" in their
# `indexOf` needles — CRLF breaks every multi-line needle match.
#
# The symptoms:
#   - `git_status_test.zig`: "could not find `is_git_repo = false` response literal"
#     (needle uses `\n        };` but file has `\r\n        };`)
#   - `set_git_worktree_test.zig`: "classifyPath signature does not match"
#     (same CRLF problem in the 4-arg form needle)
#   - Any other static-contract test that has a multi-line literal
#
# This file is read by Git on every checkout. Pair with the
# "normalize CRLF before matching" helper in the test helpers
# (see `src/ai_workflow/tui/test_text_normalize.zig` once added)
# so even if a contributor's editor sneaks CRLF in, the tests
# still pass.
#
# Pattern summary:
#   `* text=auto`       — let Git auto-detect text vs binary
#   `*.zig text eol=lf` — force LF for Zig source files (most
#                         important for static-contract tests)
#   `* text eol=lf`     — force LF for everything else
#   `*.png binary`      — explicit binary (overrides `text=auto`)
#
# See https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes for the full syntax.

*               text=auto eol=lf
*.zig           text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
*.zsh           text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.tsx           text eol=lf
*.vue           text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf

# Binary files (override `text=auto` from the first line)
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.webp          binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.eot           binary
